KNOWNBUG
temporal_assumption1.sv
--bdd
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.r -> main\.b: PROVED$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
bdd_enginet::build_BDDs (src/ebmc/bdd_engine.cpp) only adds
assumptions of the form "always p" with a state predicate p to the
transition relation, and silently ignores all other assumptions.  The
property is then checked without the assumption, and EBMC reports
REFUTED.  Assumptions that are not supported must result in an error or
in the properties being marked as inconclusive.
